<a name="bio"></a>

<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2"> <tr>
	<td class="borderbottom" colspan="2">Biography</td>
</tr> <tr>
	<td class="name">

        I hatched in a small village named Vetanda, at the goot of the Giant's
        Run Mountains in the Dragon's Coast region of Faerun.  My clan, from
        which the village got it's name, was a small clan of black Dragonborn
        that had emigrated from Tymanther some time ago.  I still remember
        those days as a youngling, in our little fishing community.  That was
        before they came.<p>

        I still remember Pyall's face as he dug me out of the pile of corpses
        left by the soldiers of Bane.  As he pulled me - sole survivor of my
        village - from all my dead kin, he smiled and told me all would be
        well.  He healed my wounds and took me from the charnel house my
        village had become.  He took me to his home, the temple of Lathander in
        Westgate.  He tought me the beliefs of Lathander: that we can make a
        difference in the world, and that with good thoughts and good deeds we
        can bring light to the dark places.  He used to joke, even on his
        deathbed, that I was a dark place that he was converting to the light,
        and that the light could shine from my dark scales just as well as his
        pale flesh.  I will always love him, and be indebted to him for saving
        my life.<p>

        I strive to do good, and to honor my adopted human father's legacy.  I
        want to help all the unfortunate, the victims, those who suffered as I
        did.  But do not misunderstand me.  I will never forgive the
        worshippers of Bane.  I think of them often.  I will punish them in due
        course. But they are nothing.  They are faceless non-beings who could
        be anyone in any village in any nation. The problem wasn't them.  It
        was me. I was weak. I could not stop them. I was helpless to resist as
        they did the worst thing I could imagine.  And I will never, ever be
        that weak again.

</td> </tr> </table>


